     <h2 class=3D"section-title" id=3D"section-comparison">
      <span aria-hidden=3D"true" class=3D"section-number">
       01
      </span>
      Database Comparison Chart
     </h2>
     <p>
      One scannable matrix of the major database families =E2=80=94 relatio=
nal, document, key-value, wide-column, graph, search, analytical, time-seri=
es, and vector =E2=80=94 against the decision criteria that actually drive =
the choice. Read the
      <strong>
       Best fit
      </strong>
      and
      <strong>
       Watch out for
      </strong>
      columns together: the mistake is almost never picking a "bad" databas=
e, it is using a good one for the wrong workload. Engine versions verified =
August 2026.
     </p>
     <div class=3D"table-tools js-only">
      <span class=3D"table-hint">
       QUICK COMPARE =C2=B7 Scroll table for more =E2=86=92
      </span>
      <button aria-pressed=3D"false" class=3D"control" id=3D"technical-togg=
le" type=3D"button">
       Show technical columns
      </button>
     </div>
     <div aria-label=3D"Database comparison, scroll horizontally for more c=
olumns" class=3D"table-responsive" role=3D"region" tabindex=3D"0">
      <table class=3D"table table-hover">
       <caption>
        Database families at a glance. Compare best fit, constraints, and e=
ngines.
       </caption>
       <thead>
        <tr>
         <th scope=3D"col">
          Family
         </th>
         <th class=3D"technical-col" scope=3D"col">
          Data model
         </th>
         <th class=3D"technical-col" scope=3D"col">
          Query / access
         </th>
         <th class=3D"technical-col" scope=3D"col">
          Consistency &amp; scaling
         </th>
         <th scope=3D"col">
          Best fit
         </th>
         <th scope=3D"col">
          Watch out for
         </th>
         <th scope=3D"col">
          Leading engines (2026)
         </th>
        </tr>
       </thead>
       <tbody>
        <tr>
         <th scope=3D"row">
          Relational (SQL)
         </th>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Tables, rows, fixed schema, foreign keys
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          SQL; rich joins &amp; ad-hoc queries
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Strong ACID; scales up, reads out via replicas; sharding is manua=
l
         </td>
         <td>
          Transactions, reporting, anything with relationships and integrit=
y rules =E2=80=94 the safe default
         </td>
         <td>
          High write throughput across many nodes; rapidly-changing schema
         </td>
         <td>
          PostgreSQL 18.4, MySQL 8.4 LTS, SQL Server 2025, MariaDB 12 LTS, =
SQLite
         </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
         <th scope=3D"row">
          Document
         </th>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Self-describing JSON/BSON documents
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Document API + secondary indexes; aggregation pipeline
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Tunable; horizontal scaling via sharding built in
         </td>
         <td>
          Evolving schemas, content/catalog data, per-entity aggregates
         </td>
         <td>
          Many-to-many joins; cross-document transactions (supported but no=
t the strength)
         </td>
         <td>
          MongoDB 8.3, Couchbase, Amazon DocumentDB
         </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
         <th scope=3D"row">
          Key-Value
         </th>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Opaque value keyed by a unique key
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          GET/SET by key; near-O(1) lookups
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          In-memory speed (sub-ms); scales horizontally; often eventual
         </td>
         <td>
          Caching, sessions, rate limiting, leaderboards, queues
         </td>
         <td>
          Querying by value or range; durable system-of-record use
         </td>
         <td>
          Redis 8.10 (tri-licensed, now AGPLv3), Valkey (BSD fork), Memcach=
ed
         </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
         <th scope=3D"row">
          Wide-Column
         </th>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Rows with dynamic column families, partitioned by key
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          CQL-style; queries must match the partition key
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Tunable consistency; linear write scaling across many nodes
         </td>
         <td>
          Massive write volume, time-ordered/IoT data, always-on multi-regi=
on
         </td>
         <td>
          Ad-hoc queries and joins =E2=80=94 you design tables per query, n=
ot per entity
         </td>
         <td>
          Apache Cassandra 5.0.8, ScyllaDB, HBase, Bigtable
         </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
         <th scope=3D"row">
          Graph
         </th>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Nodes and relationships as first-class, with properties
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Cypher / Gremlin; cheap multi-hop traversals
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Strong within a node; scaling out is harder than other families
         </td>
         <td>
          Social graphs, fraud rings, recommendations, dependency/impact an=
alysis
         </td>
         <td>
          Simple tabular data or bulk analytics over all rows
         </td>
         <td>
          Neo4j (2026.06 LTS / CalVer), Memgraph, Amazon Neptune
         </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
         <th scope=3D"row">
          Search
         </th>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Inverted-index documents with analyzers
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Full-text queries, relevance ranking, facets, aggregations
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Near-real-time; horizontally sharded; eventually consistent
         </td>
         <td>
          Text search, log/observability analytics, faceted product search
         </td>
         <td>
          System-of-record duties or strong transactional guarantees
         </td>
         <td>
          Elasticsearch 9.3.3, OpenSearch 3.6.0
         </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
         <th scope=3D"row">
          Analytical / Columnar
         </th>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Column-oriented storage, heavy compression
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          SQL scans/aggregations over billions of rows
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Read-optimized OLAP; scales scans across nodes/cores
         </td>
         <td>
          Dashboards, aggregations, event analytics, ad-hoc BI
         </td>
         <td>
          Frequent single-row updates/deletes and OLTP transactions
         </td>
         <td>
          ClickHouse 26.6, DuckDB 1.x (embedded), Apache Druid
         </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
         <th scope=3D"row">
          Time-Series
         </th>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Timestamped measurements keyed by series/tags
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          SQL or purpose-built API; downsampling &amp; retention policies
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Append-optimized; automatic partitioning by time
         </td>
         <td>
          Metrics, monitoring, sensor/IoT streams, financial ticks
         </td>
         <td>
          Relational workloads or heavy cross-entity joins
         </td>
         <td>
          TimescaleDB (on PostgreSQL), InfluxDB, Prometheus
         </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
         <th scope=3D"row">
          Vector
         </th>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          High-dimension embeddings + metadata
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Approximate nearest-neighbor (ANN) search by similarity
         </td>
         <td class=3D"technical-col">
          Index-dependent (HNSW/IVF); recall traded against latency
         </td>
         <td>
          Semantic search, RAG, recommendations, image/audio similarity
         </td>
         <td>
          Exact lookups, transactions, or when a SQL DB's vector extension =
already suffices
         </td>
         <td>
          pgvector 0.8 (in PostgreSQL), Milvus 3.0, Qdrant 1.18, Weaviate 1=
.37, Pinecone (managed)
         </td>
        </tr>
       </tbody>
      </table>
     </div>
     <p class=3D"start-note">
      <strong>
       Start here:
      </strong>
      reach for relational first and only move off it for a specific reason=
 =E2=80=94 scale, access pattern, or data shape that SQL handles poorly. Ma=
ny teams get the best of both by staying on PostgreSQL and adding an extens=
ion (JSONB for documents,
      <code>
       pgvector
      </code>
      for embeddings, TimescaleDB for time-series) before adopting a second=
 engine to operate.
     </p>
